<p>If trainers get caught up in a fight with wild Pokémon they do not think they can win against, they can attempt a group DEX check as an action on a PC’s turn, contested by the DEX ability score of the wild Pokémon involved in the combat. More PCs need to succeed than fail. Tie goes to the runner. In case of a fail, trainers may not attempt to run away again until that PC’s next turn (one full round).</p>
